## Install

The skill is the folder `skills/{{SKILL_NAME}}/`. Copy it into your agent's skills directory:

| Agent | Project scope | User scope |
|---|---|---|
| Claude Code | `.claude/skills/` | `~/.claude/skills/` |
| OpenAI Codex | `.agents/skills/` | `~/.agents/skills/` |
| OpenCode | `.opencode/skills/` | `~/.config/opencode/skills/` |
| Google Antigravity | `.agents/skills/` | `~/.gemini/config/skills/` |

Paths as documented by each vendor on {{SNAPSHOT_DATE}}.

```bash
# Example: user scope, Claude Code
cp -R skills/{{SKILL_NAME}} ~/.claude/skills/
```

Other ways to install:

- **claude.ai**: zip the folder (`cd skills && zip -r ../{{SKILL_NAME}}.zip {{SKILL_NAME}}`) and upload the zip as a custom skill in the claude.ai settings. Requires a paid plan with code execution enabled.
- **Many agents at once**: `npx skills add <owner>/<repo>` once this repository is on GitHub, or `npx skills add .` from a local clone. This uses the community [`skills` CLI](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills).

